From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:15:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: offer a depth format only where the host stores it

A sized depth internal format is a request, not a promise. glTexImage2D with
GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT32 succeeds on a host that has no 32-bit unsigned-normalized
depth at all, because GL lets it pick another depth format; Mesa's Zink, whose
Vulkan device has only D16_UNORM, D32_SFLOAT and the packed depth-stencil
formats, settles for 24 bits and reports success. vrend_add_formats() only
checks that the glTexImage2D call raised no error, so VIRGL_FORMAT_Z32_UNORM
reaches the guest as a capability the host does not have.

That is not only a texture capability to the guest. Mesa builds its EGL and GLX
config lists out of the depth formats its driver claims, preferring
PIPE_FORMAT_Z32_UNORM over PIPE_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT, so the advertised format
becomes the storage of every default framebuffer with 32 depth bits. An OpenGL
ES guest then holds a default depth buffer it cannot name -- ES has no
unsigned-normalized 32-bit depth format -- and Mesa's blit validation rejects
every blit out of it, because the only 32-bit depth format ES can name on the
other side is GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT32F and the datatypes do not match.

Probe what the host actually stored, with GL_TEXTURE_DEPTH_SIZE and
GL_TEXTURE_DEPTH_TYPE, and register the format only when both agree with the
virgl format. Nothing is lost where the host does substitute: the storage was
already the substitute, and the guest now picks VIRGL_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT, which
is 32 bits it can name. The deliberate GLES-host Z24 stand-in for Z32 is left
alone; it has its own documented contract.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_formats.c | 57 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
index 69ceb82a67917034977cd0ea9062897fa5c59187..d1db8bb999cb4de5f608869adb6eec26dc455b12 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
@@ -586,9 +586,64 @@ void vrend_build_format_list_common(void)
 }
 
 
+/* A sized depth internal format is a request, not a promise: GL lets the host
+ * satisfy GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT32 with whatever depth storage it has, and a
+ * Vulkan or Metal host has no 32-bit unsigned-normalized depth at all -- Zink
+ * settles for 24 bits and reports success.
+ *
+ * The guest cannot see that substitution, and this list is not only a texture
+ * capability to it: Mesa builds its EGL and GLX config lists out of the depth
+ * formats the driver claims, so VIRGL_FORMAT_Z32_UNORM becomes the storage of
+ * every default framebuffer with 32 depth bits. An OpenGL ES guest then cannot
+ * name its own depth buffer -- ES has no unsigned-normalized 32-bit depth
+ * format -- and every blit out of that framebuffer is rejected for a depth
+ * format mismatch.
+ *
+ * Offer such a format only where the host really has it. The guest then falls
+ * back to VIRGL_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT, which is 32 bits of storage it can name.
+ */
+static bool vrend_host_depth_storage_is_exact(GLenum internalformat,
+                                              GLenum glformat,
+                                              GLenum gltype,
+                                              GLint depth_bits,
+                                              GLint depth_type)
+{
+   GLuint tex_id;
+   GLint host_bits = 0;
+   GLint host_type = GL_NONE;
+   bool exact;
+
+   glGenTextures(1, &tex_id);
+   glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, tex_id);
+   while (glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR) {}
+
+   glTexImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, internalformat, 32, 32, 0, glformat, gltype,
+                NULL);
+   if (glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR) {
+      glGetTexLevelParameteriv(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, GL_TEXTURE_DEPTH_SIZE,
+                               &host_bits);
+      glGetTexLevelParameteriv(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, GL_TEXTURE_DEPTH_TYPE,
+                               &host_type);
+   }
+   exact = host_bits == depth_bits && host_type == depth_type;
+
+   glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0);
+   glDeleteTextures(1, &tex_id);
+   while (glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR) {}
+
+   if (!exact)
+      virgl_warn("host stores 0x%x as %d depth bits of type 0x%x, not %d of "
+                 "0x%x; not offering it to the guest\n",
+                 internalformat, host_bits, host_type, depth_bits, depth_type);
+   return exact;
+}
+
 void vrend_build_format_list_gl(void)
 {
-  add_formats(gl_z32_format);
+  if (vrend_host_depth_storage_is_exact(GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT32,
+                                        GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT, GL_UNSIGNED_INT,
+                                        32, GL_UNSIGNED_NORMALIZED))
+     add_formats(gl_z32_format);
   /* GL_BGRA formats aren't as well supported in GLES as in GL, specially in
    * transfer operations. So we only register support for it in GL.
    */
